Title: Stochastic low-frequency variability of 50 massive stars in the Cygnus OB
associations and the Small Magellanic Cloud
Authors: M. G. Pedersen and L. Bildsten
Table: Table B2: Average parameter estimates and ranges for the B20 sample
================================================================================
Byte-by-byte Description of file: table_B2.mrt
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Bytes Format Units  Label     Explanations
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  1-  9   A9     ---    TIC            TESS Input Catalog ID
 11- 14   A4     ppm^2/uHz log_alpha_0    Average fitted log10 power density at
                                    0 micro Hertz
 16- 19   A4     ppm^2/uHz e_log_alpha_0  Lower uncertainty on log_alpha_0
 21- 24   A4     ppm^2/uHz E_log_alpha_0  Upper uncertainty on log_alpha_0
 26- 30   A5     uHz    nu_char        Average characteristic frequency
 32- 36   A5     uHz    e_nu_char      Lower uncertainty on nu_char
 38- 42   A5     uHz    E_nu_char      Upper uncertainty on nu_char
 44- 47   A4     ---    gamma          Average slope of Stochastic low-frequency
                                    variability in power density
 49- 52   A4     ---    e_gamma        Lower uncertainty in gamma
 54- 57   A4     ---    E_gamma        Upper uncertainty in gamma
 59- 62   A4     ppm^2/uHz log_Cw         Average log10 of white noise in power
                                    density
 64- 67   A4     ppm^2/uHz e_log_Cw       Lower uncertainty on log_Cw
 69- 72   A4     ppm^2/uHz E_log_Cw       Upper uncertainty on log_Cw
 74- 77   A4     ppm    log_RMS        Average log10 of root-mean-squared
                                    variability of light curve
 79- 82   A4     ppm    e_log_RMS      Lower uncertainty on log_RMS
 84- 87   A4     ppm    E_log_RMS      Upper uncertainty on log_RMS
 89- 94   A6     uHz    nu_50          Average frequency at 0.5 cumulative
                                    integrated power density
 96-100   A5     uHz    e_nu_50        Lower uncertainty on nu_50
102-106   A5     uHz    E_nu_50        Upper uncertainty on nu_50
108-112   A5     ---    w              Average width of the cumulative
                                    integrated power density
114-118   A5     ---    e_w            Lower uncertainty on w
120-124   A5     ---    E_w            Upper uncertainty on w

